<title>JAPAN: Japan August silver imports up 159.7 pct year/year. [CORRECTED 04:13 GMT]</title>
<headline>Japan August silver imports up 159.7 pct year/year. [CORRECTED 04:13 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's silver imports in August were up 159.7 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>The figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    August 96     July 96	August 95</p>
<p> Total		88.57	 106.86	   34.11</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Mexico	     55.36	  36.03	   31.02</p>
<p> U.S.		  0.00	  18.66	    0.09</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first eight (corrects from seven) months of 1996 were 810.61 tonnes against 926.01 in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
